{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","commitSha":"c2534ff9c84422e00711da31629a76f3f59feb98","shard":"153ef33cb59076fa","symbols":[{"path":"xrpl/SeqProxy","kind":"class","name":"SeqProxy","qualifiedName":"xrpl::SeqProxy","scope":"xrpl","category":"production","access":"public","documentation":{"status":"present","brief":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that represents either a sequence value or a ticket value."}],"description":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"We use the "},{"type":"link","text":"value()","target":{"path":"xrpl/SeqProxy/value/da3e3939","resolution":"doxygen"}},{"type":"text","text":" of a "},{"type":"link","text":"SeqProxy","target":{"path":"xrpl/SeqProxy","resolution":"doxygen"}},{"type":"text","text":" in places where a sequence was used before. An example of this is the sequence of an Offer stored in the ledger. We do the same thing with the in-ledger identifier of a Check, "},{"type":"link","text":"Payment","target":{"path":"xrpl/Payment","resolution":"doxygen"}},{"type":"text","text":" Channel, and Escrow."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Why is this safe? If we use the "},{"type":"link","text":"SeqProxy::value()","target":{"path":"xrpl/SeqProxy/value/da3e3939","resolution":"doxygen"}},{"type":"text","text":", how do we know that each ledger entry will be unique?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"There are two components that make this safe:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"type":"text","text":"A \"TicketCreate\" transaction carefully avoids creating a ticket that corresponds with an already used Sequence or Ticket value. The transactor does this by referring to the account root's sequence number. Creating the ticket advances the account root's sequence number so the same ticket (or sequence) value cannot be used again."}],[{"type":"text","text":"When a \"TicketCreate\" transaction creates a batch of tickets it advances the account root sequence to one past the largest created ticket. Therefore all tickets in a batch other than the first may never have the same value as a sequence on that same account. And since a ticket may only be used once there will never be any duplicates within this account."}]]}],"returns":null,"notes":[],"suppressionReason":null,"inheritedFrom":null},"location":{"declaration":{"file":"include/xrpl/protocol/SeqProxy.h","line":36},"definition":{"file":"include/xrpl/protocol/SeqProxy.h","line":37,"endLine":159}},"corrections":[],"templateParameters":null,"isTemplateSpecialization":false,"isFinal":false,"isAbstract":false,"baseClasses":[],"derivedClasses":[],"friends":[],"deductionGuides":[],"nested":[],"members":["xrpl/SeqProxy/Type","xrpl/SeqProxy/value_","xrpl/SeqProxy/type_","xrpl/SeqProxy/SeqProxy/4c889e34","xrpl/SeqProxy/SeqProxy/f932b794","xrpl/SeqProxy/operator-assign/b8f6473c","xrpl/SeqProxy/value/da3e3939","xrpl/SeqProxy/isSeq/a3810c51","xrpl/SeqProxy/isTicket/a4088a26","xrpl/SeqProxy/advanceBy/b459a991","xrpl/SeqProxy/rawSequence/bff29c07","xrpl/SeqProxy/rawTicket/061f4045","xrpl/SeqProxy/operator-equal/7a4c8384","xrpl/SeqProxy/operator-less/153d1a50","xrpl/SeqProxy/operator-greater/3646cf95","xrpl/SeqProxy/operator-greater-equal/84d51e14","xrpl/SeqProxy/operator-less-equal/285e049a","xrpl/SeqProxy/operator-shift-left/7e3eef65"],"declaration":[{"text":"class SeqProxy"}]},{"path":"xrpl/SeqProxy/Type","kind":"enum","name":"Type","qualifiedName":"xrpl::SeqProxy::Type","scope":"xrpl/SeqProxy","category":"production","access":"public","documentation":{"status":"absent","brief":null,"description":[],"returns":null,"notes":[],"suppressionReason":null,"inheritedFrom":null},"location":{"declaration":{"file":"include/xrpl/protocol/SeqProxy.h","line":39},"definition":{"file":"include/xrpl/protocol/SeqProxy.h","line":39,"endLine":39}},"corrections":[],"isScoped":true,"underlyingType":[{"text":"std::uint8_t"}],"enumerators":[{"name":"Seq","initializer":[{"text":"= 0"}],"documentation":{"status":"absent","brief":null,"de